<section class="passion-section">
  <p class="section-moral">
    <em>The same system, pointed at data problems.</em>
  </p>

  <h2 id="passion">Applied analysis</h2>

  <div class="passion-intro">
    <p>Data engineering and optimization problems. Each system demonstrates a different class of technical depth: statistical modeling, API integration and solver design, signal processing under secrecy constraints.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cards-grid">
    <article class="analysis-card">
      <h3>Bears 2026 Forecast</h3>
      <p class="project-tagline">50,000-game Monte Carlo over the NFL's real 272-game schedule.</p>
      <p>Built 2026-09-09. Pipeline: ESPN schedule API → SRS from live 2025 results (measured home-field +2.18 points) → turnover-luck regression (60% nonpersistent) → roster deltas from Sleeper and web research → 50,000 simulations seeding full NFC playoff field. Explicitly not calibrated to Vegas (market: 9.5, model: 7.33 wins). Every statistic and judgment is sourced and labeled in the output.</p>
      <ul class="facts-list">
        <li>50,000 seasons simulated with stochastic tiebreaker seeding</li>
        <li>272-game base dataset, live current roster, ESPN API pipeline</li>
        <li>Turnover-luck regression (4.0 points per net turnover, 60% year-to-year decay)</li>
        <li>Game-by-game win probability and playoff odds with explicit uncertainty bounds</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="card-link"><a href="https://claude.ai/code/artifact/c6195412-507a-45cf-856e-ae33d7374137" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="cta-link">Live forecast →</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="analysis-card">
      <h3>Psinasty Power Rankings</h3>
      <p class="project-tagline">12-team superflex dynasty league scoring via Sleeper API and optimal-lineup solver.</p>
      <p>Built 2026-09-09. System: Sleeper API rosters and projections through this league's exact scoring dictionary → injury filtering → optimal-lineup solver (maximize points subject to roster constraints) → composite ranking (60% projected starters + 12% bench depth + 28% dynasty asset value). No guesswork on lineup efficiency or what "deep" means; the solver is the truth table.</p>
      <ul class="facts-list">
        <li>Optimal lineup generation subject to superflex, 2 FLEX, injury constraints</li>
        <li>Composite weighting balances production, depth bench strength, and multi-year value</li>
        <li>Sleeper API integration with this league's PPR + 0.5 TE premium, 4-point passing TD</li>
        <li>Injury status exclusion from optimal lineups; full roster depth chart</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="card-link"><a href="https://claude.ai/code/artifact/9a7e5136-1c06-46ab-b97e-ffffefe9eaf5" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="cta-link">Live rankings →</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="analysis-card">
      <h3>Tuono — Estimating Hidden State</h3>
      <p class="project-tagline">Signal processing and state estimation where the API refuses to return the value.</p>
      <p>World of Warcraft rotation advisor using set-membership estimation: level-crossing sampling of threshold crossings (when a boolean flag flips, that instant reveals the hidden value exactly) → Kalman-like predict/update with set-membership semantics → interval width that shrinks with observation density. 183 behavioral tests; every fix must turn its covering test red against the broken code before it counts. The math is published, the bounds are rendered, and the uncertainty is never papered over.</p>
      <ul class="facts-list">
        <li>Level-crossing sampling (transition times yield sub-quantizer accuracy)</li>
        <li>Set-membership Kalman filter with bounded-error semantics (Schweppe/Witsenhausen)</li>
        <li>Soundness-preserving width floor to prevent covariance collapse; no confidently-wrong answers</li>
        <li>Abstract interpretation: every output is a three-valued predicate (yes/no/maybe), never a lie</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="card-link"><a href="https://github.com/matt82198/Tuono" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="cta-link">github.com/matt82198/Tuono →</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

